{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtJJw1QgeXpHKsnnX2DQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The pattern is very clear. The cut answers are degenerate verbatim loops: a median of 99.6% of lines in their second half are exact repeats of earlier lines, against about 4% in finished answers. There is no language drift (non-ASCII is about 0). In 57% of cut answers the correct answer appears very early (median at 2.4% of the text). So the dominant failure, accounting for nearly all 448 failures, is a repetition attractor: once the model starts re-verifying, it locks into copying its own earlier lines, and the presence penalty cannot break that because every looped token has already been penalized. Next I'll characterize the loops: the token position where looping starts, the loop period in lines, and what the looped content looks like. That tells me what to measure in a teacher-forced pass and how long the analysis texts must be.\n\n```python\n# Characterize loops: onset position (tokens), period (lines), and a short excerpt of the looped unit\ndef loop_stats(t):\n    lines=[l.strip() for l in t.split('\\n') if l.strip()]\n    seen=set(); rep=[]\n    for l in lines:\n        rep.append(l in seen); seen.add(l)\n    rep=np.array(rep,dtype=float)\n    # onset: earliest i such that mean(rep[i:i+200]) > 0.9 and stays (check the rest >0.9)\n    n=len(lines); onset=None\n    suffix_mean = np.cumsum(rep[::-1])[::-1]/np.arange(n,0,-1)\n    for i in range(n):\n        if suffix_mean[i]>0.95: onset=i; break\n    # period: look at last 400 lines, find smallest p with lines[-k]==lines[-k-p] for most k\n    tail=lines[-400:]; period=None\n    for p in range(1,200):\n        match=np.mean([tail[k]==tail[k-p] for k in range(p,len(tail))])\n        if match>0.9: period=p; break\n    # char position of onset\n    if onset is not None:\n        target=lines[onset]; cpos=t.find(target)  # approximate (first occurrence could be earlier); use cumulative\n        # better: cumulative char position via iterating\n        c=0; k=0\n        for ln in t.split('\\n'):\n            if ln.strip():\n                if k==onset: break\n                k+=1\n            c+=len(ln)+1\n        cpos=c\n    else: cpos=None\n    return onset, period, cpos, n\nL=[]\nfor r in rows:\n    for s in r['samples']:\n        if s['cut']:\n            on,p,cpos,n=loop_stats(s['text'])\n            L.append(dict(id=r['id'],onset_line=on,period=p,onset_char=cpos,nlines=n,nchar=len(s['text'])))\nL=pd.DataFrame(L)\nL['onset_tok_est']=L.onset_char/ (L.nchar/32768)\nprint(L.onset_tok_est.describe().round(0).to_dict())\nprint('period quantiles', L.period.describe().to_dict())\nprint(L.period.value_counts().head(15).to_dict())\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1494,"cache_read_input_tokens":36410,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1494},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62565e73-02d6-44c2-a0dc-003a43867133","uuid":"c16a8c88-dade-4487-9470-3c8cf5aeb354","timestamp":"2026-11-10T00:27:39.795Z","request_id":"req_011CgtJJvpVwsDE3srY3uDYD"}
